1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,862
Business Case 05 begins when a bounded high-volume recruiting program is
approved.

2
00:00:05,862 --> 00:00:11,235
A capacity-controlled cohort has explained membership, owned exceptions
and reconciled evidence.

3
00:00:11,235 --> 00:00:13,678
The governed record is HVC-001.

4
00:00:13,678 --> 00:00:19,051
The accountable actors are Volume Recruiter, Coordinator, Event Staff,
Candidate, Interviewer.

5
00:00:19,051 --> 00:00:26,379
This demonstration uses synthetic browser-memory data and creates no
database, provider, message or external-system effect.

6
00:00:26,379 --> 00:00:31,826
The action-level data-flow diagram defines 5 processes before product
navigation.

7
00:00:31,826 --> 00:00:41,631
Every process identifies the actor, screen, action, input, output,
business object, event, governed store, rule, denial and recovery.

8
00:00:41,631 --> 00:00:47,079
The highlighted path keeps each business grain and version distinct.

9
00:00:47,079 --> 00:00:50,307
Process 1, Volume Recruiter: Version the program.

10
00:00:50,307 --> 00:00:56,302
The action define population and owners produces program version in the
Program ledger.

11
00:00:56,302 --> 00:00:59,069
Process 2, Coordinator: Plan human capacity.

12
00:00:59,069 --> 00:01:04,603
The action simulate capacity produces cohort capacity plan in the
Planning ledger.

13
00:01:04,603 --> 00:01:07,370
Process 3, Coordinator: Preview bounded batch.

14
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:14,749
The action explain selection and suppression produces selected,
suppressed and exception rows in the Cohort ledger.

15
00:01:14,749 --> 00:01:17,977
Process 4, Coordinator: Confirm, cancel or retry.

16
00:01:17,977 --> 00:01:25,356
The action create bounded work produces invitations or tasks plus
per-row receipts in the Execution ledger.

17
00:01:25,356 --> 00:01:28,585
Process 5, Volume Recruiter: Reconcile cohort outcome.

18
00:01:28,585 --> 00:01:35,502
The action inspect conversion and exceptions produces denominator-bound
metrics and drill-through in the Analytics store.

19
00:01:35,502 --> 00:01:38,492
The actual product route is
/hr/high-volume/HVC-001/cohorts/COH-DEMO-001.

20
00:01:38,492 --> 00:01:46,464
It presents high-volume batch preview, undo and partial-failure board in
the surrounding recruitment or onboarding workspace.

21
00:01:46,464 --> 00:01:58,921
The screen remains a wireframe, but its identifiers, current state,
navigation, data relationships and action boundaries match the business
contract used by the connected workbench.

22
00:01:58,921 --> 00:02:02,267
The seeded workbench follows record BAT-DEMO-001.

23
00:02:02,267 --> 00:02:17,323
Its governed fields are Program, HVC-001 , Fall campus; Population
snapshot, 110 candidates; Selected, 96; Suppressed, 14 , explained;
Capacity, 12 sessions × 8; Idempotency key, BAT-HVC001-V05.

24
00:02:17,323 --> 00:02:27,918
Field classifications remain visible so the presenter can distinguish
public, internal, confidential and restricted projections for the active
persona.

25
00:02:27,918 --> 00:02:32,017
With Recruiter selected, we perform confirm bounded batch of 96.

26
00:02:32,017 --> 00:02:37,757
The guard requires every selected and suppressed row is explained; no
ranking or disposition.

27
00:02:37,757 --> 00:02:49,236
The state changes from Previewed to 89 delivered · 7 recoverable,
records BatchExecuted, writes to the Execution ledger, and creates the
handoff: Event staff receives owned check-in work.

28
00:02:49,236 --> 00:02:53,573
We now exercise the controlled exception: Simulate 7 delivery failures.

29
00:02:53,573 --> 00:02:58,344
The prepared failure is Seven provider failures after 89 successful
deliveries.

30
00:02:58,344 --> 00:03:07,452
Unsupported downstream work stops, successful prior evidence remains
intact, and the state-change receipt assigns explicit recovery without
hiding the failed attempt.

31
00:03:07,452 --> 00:03:10,876
The owned recovery is Retry failed rows idempotently.

32
00:03:10,876 --> 00:03:15,158
It reuses the governed business context without duplicating completed
effects.

33
00:03:15,158 --> 00:03:20,723
The new receipt preserves previous state, current state, actor, event
and correlation key.

34
00:03:20,723 --> 00:03:30,569
The control center and handoff inbox then expose the same recovery
through batch success, suppression, cancellation and duplicate
prevention and minimum-context next-actor work.

35
00:03:30,569 --> 00:03:32,837
Business Case 05 is complete.

36
00:03:32,837 --> 00:03:45,993
We demonstrated the level-two process contract, the actual product
route, governed field projections, the primary state transition, a
controlled exception, targeted recovery, causal dashboard evidence and
the next-actor handoff.

37
00:03:45,993 --> 00:03:50,983
A capacity-controlled cohort has explained membership, owned exceptions
and reconciled evidence.

38
00:03:50,983 --> 00:03:55,972
Production identity, persistence, integrations and external delivery
remain separate implementation gates.
